exam: It is given that {a} draws {x} triangles, {y} squares, {z} pentagons and {h} hexagons. Determine the aggregate number of sides of the said figures.
exam: Ascertain the total number of corners possessed by {x.words} triangles, {y.words} squares, {z.words} pentagons and {h.words} hexagons.
exam: Whereas a page displays {h} hexagons, {z} pentagons, {y} squares and {x} triangles, state the number of sides of all the figures taken together.
exam: Compute the total count of vertices of a collection comprising {x} triangles, {y} squares, {z} pentagons and {h} hexagons.
exercise: Grandpa passed away and left a box of tiles: {x} triangles, {y} squares, {z} pentagons and {h} hexagons. How many sides do the tiles have in all?
exercise: {a} made "an honest mistake" and counted only the squares. The page has {x} triangles, {y} squares, {z} pentagons and {h} hexagons. How many sides are there really in all?
